PARITY — web source reproduced 1:1
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Data (P1/S8 seam, no view HTTP): useTeslaEnergySites -> sites[0].energy_site_id;
  useTeslaEnergyHistory(siteId,'day',since=today−30d) -> {timestamp, solar_energy_wh}.
  kWh = solar_energy_wh/1000 (SI read directly; convert only at display). today
  matched on UTC yyyy-MM-dd bucket.

  States (every one renders — no hidden surfaces):
    loading  -> stat+chart skeleton chrome
    noSite   -> "No Tesla Energy site linked" (web first if-branch; precedence kept)
    content+hasData      -> stat row (+ area chart in standard/wide)
    content+!hasData     -> "No solar data" empty (web WidgetChartSummary isEmpty)
    error    -> QueryError-equivalent + Retry affordance
    stale    -> amber freshness chip + "Data may be stale — refreshing" banner
    offline  -> muted chip + "Offline — showing last known production" banner

  Layouts: compact (cols<=1: Today + Daily Avg, no chart) / standard (cols>=2:
  Today + 30-Day Total + Daily Avg + area chart) / wide (cols>=3: denser x ticks),
  mirroring web isCompact/isWide.

  Chart: Recharts AreaChart -> Swift Charts AreaMark+LineMark, chartSeriesEnergy
  amber stroke + top->bottom fade gradient (web #facc15 0.4->0), x ticks mapped to
  "M/D" labels, y ticks whole kWh.

  i18n (P1/S10 facade, table "SolarProductionWidget", no literals in code):
  parity keys title / noSite / noData / today / avg / total30d / solar; plus
  description + native chrome (unitKwh, fresh/stale/offline, refresh/retry/open,
  loading/errorTitle/hints/banners, chartA11y).

  Telemetry (P1/S11): start() emits view.opened surface="SolarProductionWidget".
  A11y: VoiceOver summary (Today/Daily Avg/30-Day Total + kWh), Dynamic Type via
  Font.TS roles, Reduce-Motion via shared skeleton/animation tokens.

  Intentional parity refinement (documented): shortDate formats the daily bucket's
  OWN calendar date (M/D) rather than the viewer-local re-parse, so a midnight-UTC
  bucket is never shifted a day by the device time zone.

